    "customfield_12314131": null,
    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12399062/comment/12608289",
          "id": "12608289",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Instead of interning the local part of the name but still creating new Name instances I'd rather see the NameFactory maintain a set of flywheel Name instances for commonly used names. Then we perhaps wouldn't even need to intern the namespace strings!",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2008-06-26T06:14:35.118+0000",
          "updated": "2008-06-26T06:14:35.118+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12399062/comment/12608329",
          "id": "12608329",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stefan%40jira",
            "name": "stefan@jira",
            "key": "stefan@jira",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stefan Guggisberg",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "at one point we actually did intern the local Name part. we ran into the said perm space issues at some installations, that's why we only intern the namespace uri. that helped to considerable improve performance (equals() method) and reduce memory footprint.\n\ntherefore, -1 for interning local name strings\n\ni agree with jukka that NameFactory maintaining a chache of commonly used names would be a good alternative.\nhowever, unless there's a real issue, i'd prefer to stick with interning namespace uri's.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=stefan%40jira",
            "name": "stefan@jira",
            "key": "stefan@jira",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Stefan Guggisberg",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2008-06-26T08:04:13.074+0000",
          "updated": "2008-06-26T08:04:13.074+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12399062/comment/12608457",
          "id": "12608457",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rpuch",
            "name": "rpuch",
            "key": "rpuch",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468"
            },
            "displayName": "Roman Puchkovskiy",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Samara"
          },
          "body": "We have a big repository with several tenths of thousands of nodes (which have versions). Each node has 4 reference properties.\nI'm now looking at our application heap snapshot. Its overall size is 400+ mb and almost 200 mb are strings (nearly 1.4 million of them). Most of those strings are in NameImpl instances (more than 1.3 million of instances). And nearly 1.3 million of strings are actually duplicates of 8 different strings which are local names and full names of our 4 reference properties.\nSo I think it's a real issue that needs to be resolved :) Our use case is an example when Jackrabbit uses memory inefficiently.\n\nJukka's suggestion looks much better than mine: consider 1.3 million of NameImpl instances in the example.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rpuch",
            "name": "rpuch",
            "key": "rpuch",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rpuch&avatarId=48468"
            },
            "displayName": "Roman Puchkovskiy",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Samara"
          },
          "created": "2008-06-26T14:44:58.477+0000",
          "updated": "2008-06-26T14:44:58.477+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12399062/comment/12608556",
          "id": "12608556",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130"
            },
            "displayName": "Jukka Zitting",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Do you have a chance of trying out the attached patch (JCR-1663.patch)? It's a rather simple implementation of the flyweight pattern with the added twist that it uses a fixed-size hash table to avoid blowing up too much memory in the worst case.\n\nThe change seems to work fine (i.e. no regressions), but I don't have a good performance/memory test suite at hand to verify whether this is worth the added complexity.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=jukkaz",
            "name": "jukkaz",
            "key": "jukkaz",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=jukkaz&avatarId=15130",
